# Orders close at 10:30, and the late ones need a second list
<callout icon="🧭" color="green_bg">
	The caterer needs 45 minutes of warning, so lunch orders close at 10:30. Few orders come later, 4 in 100, but each one is refused today. A second list at 11:15 would feed them, and it waits on the caterer's answer.
</callout>
### What you decide after reading
1. Rule on the cutoff: 10:30 or 11:00.
2. Ask the caterer whether it takes a second list at 11:15.
![Staff place an order, it joins the day's list, the list goes to the caterer at the cutoff, and an order after the cutoff is refused.](stills/index-figure-flow.png)
**An order waits at two steps, and only the cutoff decides whether it is late.** The order log stamps each order when it reaches the list.
